WEBVTT

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.944
Who left their dirty plate
in the replicator? Tom?

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.609
It wasn't me.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.947
It's a biohazard!

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:20.951
Take it easy!

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.749
We'll decontaminate you
when we get back home.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.221
If I ever volunteer

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.258
for a two-week
away mission again,

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.124
would somebody please
confine me to Sick Bay?

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.322
Too much togetherness
for you, Harry?

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.831
Nothing personal, Commander.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.161
To tell you the truth,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.259
I've enjoyed
our little junket together.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.531
It's given the four of us
a chance to bond.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.594
The bonding stopped

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.196
when the sonic shower
went off-line.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.764
That's all part
of the experience,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.968
the adventure.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.239
Think of the great explorers
that came before us.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.143
They survived
without creature comforts.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.114
I wouldn't want to bunk
with them, either.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.980
Now, there's a sight
for sore eyes.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.154
Delta Flyer to Voyager.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.416
We're on our approach.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.457
We've kept a candle

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.651
burning in the window for you.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.660
Forget the candles.
Break out the champagne!

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.696
I take it
the mission was a success.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.890
15 planets scanned in 14 days.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.830
We've got a cargo hold

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.267
overflowing
with dilithium ore.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.100
That's the kind of news
I like to hear.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.449
The explorers return.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.779
Welcome home.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.786
I should go away more often.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.185
I'm not going anywhere

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.620
for a long, long time.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.679
Homesick, Harry?

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.453
Well, let's just say
I'm looking forward

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.187
to a hot shower and
a comfortable bed.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.193
Don't forget to stop

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.627
by Sick Bay for your checkup.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.686
Checkup? For what?

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.959
Away team protocol.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.694
Crew members are required
to submit to a physical

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.964
if the mission lasts
more than two weeks.

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.005
Now... who's first?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.172
I'll let you know

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.367
in the morning, Doctor.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.502
Why put off till tomorrow
what you can do today...

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.807
Commander?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.507
Mr. Paris?

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.244
I've been working
on a little surprise for you.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.808
Oh! Naughty or nice?

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:00.818
Close your eyes.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.115
I like it already.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.791
Come on.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.825
So, what do you think?

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.261
A television set!

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.767
Circa 1956.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.234
I replicated the components,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.736
but I assembled it myself.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.236
This... is the remote control.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.604
You select
what you want to watch

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.664
by pressing this button.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:26.211
A slight problem.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.839
There were no remote
controls in the 1950s.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.815
I took a little
poetic license.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.945
Cartoon!

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.579
I found them
in the ship's database.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.352
Vacuum action!

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.452
Mop, mop

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.690
Don't stop...

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:45.696
What's that?

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:46.959
Now, that is called a "jingle."

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.227
According to the research
I did, they inserted them

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.963
into the entertainment
programs.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:54.596
I know, it's confusing,
but I kept them in

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.301
for authenticity.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.367
I even replicated popcorn.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.173
Aw...

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.111
Mm!

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.911
Everything is perfect,

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.917
except for one tiny detail.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.213
What?

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.845
You forgot the beer.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.514
I can fix that.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.289
You didn't miss much
while you were away.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.591
The Doctor gave a lecture

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.895
on "Insects Indigenous
to the Delta Quadrant."

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.127
Uh-huh.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.328
It was pretty boring...

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.200
until Ensign Farley
started snoring,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.501
and then no one could
keep a straight face.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.838
Of course, the Doctor
wasn't at all amused.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.433
Oh!

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.808
Hockey.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.279
It was a shame

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.872
that we had to cut
the lecture short,

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.144
but the warp
core overloaded,

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.276
and then the Borg invaded,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.944
and... we were all assimilated.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.248
Mm-hmm.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.949
You haven't heard a single thing
I've said, have you?

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.958
Oh! Look at that!

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.061
Maybe this was a bad idea.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.956
It's Eliot Ness!

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.363
Come on out!
We don't want any trouble!

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.596
We're the Barkers!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.638
You're never going to get us!

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.151
We're under attack.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:16.313
Stay down!

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.186
Keep moving!

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.716
Somebody cover me!

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.580
Need a medic over here!

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.491
Move it!

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:48.966
Stay low!

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.238
Aah!

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.408
Hold your fire!

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:02.215
I said hold your fire!

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:03.915
I need a medic!

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:15.701
Keep moving!

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:17.625
Keep moving!

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.199
Tom?

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:25.366
Tom?

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:28.973
- Tom?
- Mm.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.410
Must've been one
hell of a dream.

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:37.084
I was...

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.589
I was in the middle
of a battlefield.

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:41.252
I was grazed right...

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.887
right here.

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:48.194
They always said television
was a bad influence.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:49.894
How about a nice cartoon?

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.527
That should chase
away the nightmare.

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:52.901
No!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.373
No, I think I've had enough.

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.289
Stay down!

00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.027
Stay low!

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:09.644
It sounds like you had
an anxiety attack.

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.013
I've never been
claustrophobic before.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.779
There's a first time
for everything.

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:18.446
Do you know
what could've caused it?

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.650
Let's see...

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:20.987
you spend two weeks
on an away mission,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.857
working 18-hour days.

00:09:22.929 --> 00:09:24.897
Then, as soon as you
return to Voyager,

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.591
you become "Ensign Eager,"

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:28.031
back on duty and rarin' to go.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.897
I had work to do.

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:31.095
There was a plasma
leak on Deck 5.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.297
Plasma leak
or no plasma leak,

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.306
you're suffering
from exhaustion.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.672
I'm recommending you take
the next two days off.

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:38.767
But I...

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.903
I can always make it three.

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.106
You win.

00:09:43.182 --> 00:09:44.809
Guess I am pretty tired.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:51.350
Ah.

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:58.420
Welcome back.

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:02.157
Hello.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.895
Did you have a good trip?

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.494
Wonderful, thank you.

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:08.503
You look tired.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:11.737
Oh, no. It's just
a little shuttle lag.

00:10:11.811 --> 00:10:13.335
Don't you have
a geometry lesson?

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:14.845
You don't want to keep
your teacher waiting.

00:10:14.914 --> 00:10:15.846
Seven of Nine assigned me

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:17.644
a special project.

00:10:17.717 --> 00:10:19.776
I'm supposed to build
a tetragon,

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:20.944
but I have to use
everyday things.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.045
I'm not allowed
to use a replicator.

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:28.119
I was thinking about using
some vegetables

00:10:28.194 --> 00:10:29.354
from the Airponics Bay.

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.555
Carrots and celery?

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:34.926
Neelix?

00:10:35.001 --> 00:10:37.697
Carrots and celery.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.364
A good idea.

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:41.565
Will you help me?

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:45.338
Uh... I don't think
I'll have time today.

00:10:45.411 --> 00:10:47.038
Tonight?

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:51.245
I don't think that I'll
have time then, either.

00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:52.614
A lot of work to do!

00:10:52.685 --> 00:10:54.414
Well, then,
why don't I help you?

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.187
What's cooking?

00:10:59.258 --> 00:10:59.917
Ouch!

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.187
Let me see your hand!

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:03.091
I'm okay.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.026
Your hand!

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:05.393
We've got to get
you to Sick Bay.

00:11:05.464 --> 00:11:06.522
I'm fine.

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:07.964
Sick Bay!

00:11:09.235 --> 00:11:10.532
That's the best joke
I've ever heard.

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:11.831
Get down. Stay behind me.

00:11:11.904 --> 00:11:12.836
What?!

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:14.463
I said get down!

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:19.500
Go, go! Quickly!

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:23.244
Come on! Help me with this!

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:31.482
Keep moving!

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:34.158
Try not to move.

00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:35.250
Get away from me!

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:36.521
I can help you.

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:39.894
I don't... want your help!

00:11:42.935 --> 00:11:45.233
We need help over here!

00:11:51.277 --> 00:11:52.209
Hold your fire.

00:11:52.278 --> 00:11:53.643
I said hold your fire!

00:11:53.713 --> 00:11:55.408
We're under attack, sir!

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:56.413
Saavdra... where is he?

00:11:56.482 --> 00:11:57.608
I think he's at base.

00:12:04.957 --> 00:12:06.322
We were supposed to
evacuate the colony,

00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:07.359
not destroy it!

00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:10.623
That was before the Nakan
started shooting.

00:12:10.696 --> 00:12:12.561
They're civilians!

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:15.156
Civilians
with particle weapons.

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:16.462
Tuvok to Commander Chakotay.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.931
Commander, please respond.

00:12:20.039 --> 00:12:21.063
Go ahead.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.233
We have a security breach
in the Mess Hall.

00:12:26.445 --> 00:12:27.776
I'm on my way.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.347
Tell them to call off
the attack!

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:32.149
Put down your weapon, Neelix.

00:12:32.218 --> 00:12:33.207
Let us help you.

00:12:33.285 --> 00:12:34.377
Stay away!

00:12:34.453 --> 00:12:37.115
I won't let you hurt her!

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:39.521
Get back!

00:12:41.894 --> 00:12:43.828
He appears to be hallucinating.

00:12:45.831 --> 00:12:46.855
Neelix!

00:12:46.932 --> 00:12:48.866
This is Commander Chakotay!

00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:50.162
Let Naomi go!

00:12:50.236 --> 00:12:51.635
No one's going to hurt her!

00:12:51.704 --> 00:12:53.365
That's an order!

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:55.168
No!

00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:56.299
Not until Saavdra's called off

00:12:56.375 --> 00:12:58.741
his attack.

00:12:58.811 --> 00:13:00.369
There's a back entrance
to the galley.

00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:01.606
If you can distract
him, perhaps...

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.011
I want to try
something first.

00:13:06.585 --> 00:13:07.643
Neelix!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.814
Listen to me. It's okay.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.552
Saavdra ordered a cease-fire.

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:14.923
The colony's secure.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.028
The battle's over.

00:13:19.198 --> 00:13:21.098
Why do I still
hear weapons fire?

00:13:23.269 --> 00:13:24.930
It's just a few soldiers.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.059
They're celebrating.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:27.435
The battle's over.

00:13:31.277 --> 00:13:33.245
Neelix, please.

00:13:33.312 --> 00:13:34.939
I'll protect Naomi.

00:13:37.249 --> 00:13:39.046
How do I know
you won't trick me?

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:43.054
Because I'm on your side.

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:45.090
I want to end this conflict
as much as you do.

00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:48.316
Let her go.

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:50.453
It's safe now.

00:13:50.529 --> 00:13:51.996
The killing's over.

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:34.403
I gave him
a mild sedative.

00:14:34.473 --> 00:14:36.338
Any idea what caused
the delusions?

00:14:36.408 --> 00:14:39.935
His norepinephrine levels are
three times what they should be.

00:14:40.079 --> 00:14:42.673
Neurochemically speaking,
he's suffering from a form

00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:45.182
of post-traumatic
stress syndrome.

00:14:45.251 --> 00:14:48.049
I dreamed I was fighting
in an alien war.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:51.578
The same war Neelix
seemed to be reliving.

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:52.749
Harry Kim was in earlier.

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:54.622
He had an anxiety attack.

00:14:54.693 --> 00:14:56.923
I haven't spoken
with Mr. Paris yet.

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:59.863
Three members
of the same away team.

00:14:59.932 --> 00:15:01.991
Did you run into any kind
of trouble while you were gone?

00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:02.999
None.

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:04.296
The mission was by the book.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:07.897
Your engramatic activities
contradict that, Commander.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.507
These are real memories,

00:15:09.575 --> 00:15:11.668
not mere dreams
or hallucinations.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:13.405
Maybe you were abducted...

00:15:13.479 --> 00:15:15.447
manipulated into fighting.

00:15:15.514 --> 00:15:18.449
Our memories have been
tampered with before.

00:15:18.517 --> 00:15:21.611
We're going to retrace
your mission.

00:15:21.687 --> 00:15:22.619
Start reviewing

00:15:22.688 --> 00:15:24.679
the Delta Flyer sensor logs.

00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:26.588
See if you come up
with anything unusual.

00:15:26.659 --> 00:15:28.820
How long before Neelix
is back on his feet?

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.691
I can wake him now
if you'd like.

00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:32.424
Do it.

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:36.294
Each of you seems to hold
a piece of the puzzle.

00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:39.895
Let's see if we can start
putting them together.

00:15:39.972 --> 00:15:43.738
I don't remember much,
just bits and pieces.

00:15:43.809 --> 00:15:48.303
I dreamt I was on a planet
in the middle of a battle.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.211
I have no idea
how I got there.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:51.214
I can't remember.

00:15:51.283 --> 00:15:52.307
When I was in the Jefferies

00:15:52.384 --> 00:15:56.548
tube, I heard
weapons fire, screams.

00:15:56.622 --> 00:15:58.249
People were screaming.

00:15:58.324 --> 00:16:00.315
I got
so frightened.

00:16:00.392 --> 00:16:01.689
Of what?

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.387
I... I don't know.

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:04.895
I remember getting shot.

00:16:04.997 --> 00:16:07.557
There's no evidence
of a wound.

00:16:07.633 --> 00:16:10.033
If our memories were wiped,

00:16:10.102 --> 00:16:13.401
our physical injuries
could have been masked as well.

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:16.270
Do any of you recall
who you were fighting?

00:16:16.342 --> 00:16:18.071
It was dark.

00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:20.111
I couldn't see them very well.

00:16:20.179 --> 00:16:21.578
They were firing at us.

00:16:21.647 --> 00:16:25.014
The Naka... Na... Nakana...

00:16:25.084 --> 00:16:27.109
Nakan.

00:16:27.186 --> 00:16:28.346
They were called the Nakan.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.352
Right.

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:31.651
Right.

00:16:31.724 --> 00:16:34.215
They... they lived
in a remote colony.

00:16:34.293 --> 00:16:36.784
We were trying
to evacuate them.

00:16:36.862 --> 00:16:39.262
But they were fighting us.

00:16:39.331 --> 00:16:42.391
Why couldn't they just
do what they were told?

00:16:42.468 --> 00:16:43.696
We had no right to be there!

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:45.134
It was for
their own good.

00:16:45.204 --> 00:16:47.172
Gentlemen, stay focused.

00:16:47.239 --> 00:16:49.935
You said you were trying
to evacuate their colony.

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:50.941
Why?

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.035
Those were our orders.

00:16:53.112 --> 00:16:54.204
Who gave them?

00:16:55.814 --> 00:16:57.805
Saavdra.

00:16:57.883 --> 00:16:59.783
Commander Saavdra.

00:16:59.852 --> 00:17:00.910
He was in charge of our unit.

00:17:00.986 --> 00:17:02.214
We were part
of an attack force.

00:17:02.287 --> 00:17:04.050
You were coerced?

00:17:04.123 --> 00:17:05.249
No!

00:17:05.324 --> 00:17:06.416
No, I volunteered.

00:17:06.492 --> 00:17:07.459
We all did.

00:17:07.526 --> 00:17:09.460
I find that difficult
to believe.

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:10.893
You were obviously
manipulated somehow.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:16.058
No! No, no, no, no,
I remember now.

00:17:16.135 --> 00:17:19.366
We held a, uh, a briefing
to plan the evacuation.

00:17:19.438 --> 00:17:20.735
You were there, Commander.

00:17:20.806 --> 00:17:21.773
Mr. Paris!

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.671
It was a command post.

00:17:23.742 --> 00:17:24.674
That's right.

00:17:24.743 --> 00:17:27.109
It was night, 0200 hours.

00:17:27.179 --> 00:17:30.012
We'd been awake for days.

00:17:32.651 --> 00:17:33.743
We were exhausted.

00:17:33.852 --> 00:17:36.252
What do our spotters report?

00:17:36.321 --> 00:17:37.253
The Nakan are unarmed.

00:17:37.322 --> 00:17:38.448
They won't put up a fight.

00:17:38.524 --> 00:17:40.924
Once we've disabled
their shield generators,

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:43.655
we'll deploy Units 5 and 6.

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:47.563
They may be unarmed, but they
won't be happy to see us.

00:17:47.633 --> 00:17:49.157
Don't provoke them.

00:17:49.234 --> 00:17:52.692
I want to come out of this
with zero casualties

00:17:52.771 --> 00:17:54.204
on both sides.

00:17:54.273 --> 00:17:55.865
Understood.

00:17:55.941 --> 00:17:58.136
The perimeter is the weakest
in Sector 14.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.234
The terrain's very flat.

00:17:59.311 --> 00:18:01.939
It's an ideal landing spot
for transports.

00:18:02.014 --> 00:18:03.675
Once we've secured the village,

00:18:03.749 --> 00:18:05.114
take the colonists there.

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:06.208
Get them aboard.

00:18:06.285 --> 00:18:08.310
Do your best to reassure them.

00:18:08.387 --> 00:18:11.879
Make them understand that this
is a temporary relocation,

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:13.889
that they're going
to be back there

00:18:14.026 --> 00:18:15.186
within a few weeks.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.488
Understood.

00:18:16.562 --> 00:18:19.554
Yes, sir! Aye, aye, sir.

00:18:21.767 --> 00:18:22.893
Problem?

00:18:23.035 --> 00:18:24.525
Just one.

00:18:24.603 --> 00:18:26.901
This unit could
use a little sleep.

00:18:26.972 --> 00:18:28.735
I suggest we wait
until daybreak.

00:18:28.807 --> 00:18:30.900
I promised Command
we'd have this colony

00:18:30.976 --> 00:18:32.170
secured today.

00:18:32.244 --> 00:18:33.472
It can wait a few hours.

00:18:33.545 --> 00:18:36.207
I'm sorry.

00:18:36.281 --> 00:18:40.445
But when this mission's over,
how does a week

00:18:40.519 --> 00:18:42.350
on Toranius Prime sound?

00:18:42.421 --> 00:18:44.048
Never been there.

00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:47.650
Compared to this place,
it's paradise.

00:18:49.294 --> 00:18:50.226
The mission proceeded

00:18:50.295 --> 00:18:51.922
as planned.

00:18:51.997 --> 00:18:54.363
We disabled their
shield generators

00:18:54.433 --> 00:18:55.730
and entered the colony.

00:18:55.801 --> 00:18:56.927
We were rounding up the Nakan.

00:18:57.069 --> 00:19:00.061
To be honest, I expected them to
give us a little more trouble.

00:19:00.139 --> 00:19:02.198
But then we came
to the last enclosure.

00:19:02.274 --> 00:19:04.174
Do you remember
the last enclosure?

00:19:04.243 --> 00:19:05.505
It was empty.

00:19:05.577 --> 00:19:07.204
Where were they?

00:19:07.279 --> 00:19:08.610
They were supposed
to be there.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.477
24 colonists unaccounted for.

00:19:10.549 --> 00:19:12.483
We thought the spotters
had made a mistake.

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:14.849
We should've known
something was wrong.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.683
We should've gotten out then.

00:19:16.755 --> 00:19:17.687
This way.

00:19:17.756 --> 00:19:19.348
Stay in line.

00:19:19.424 --> 00:19:21.221
Keep moving.

00:19:21.293 --> 00:19:23.193
Evacuation detail to base.

00:19:23.262 --> 00:19:24.286
We're ready for transport.

00:19:24.363 --> 00:19:26.263
Transports on approach.

00:19:26.331 --> 00:19:27.298
Keep moving.

00:19:27.366 --> 00:19:28.731
I have to find my husband.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:29.732
Don't worry.

00:19:29.801 --> 00:19:31.530
He'll be on one
of the transports.

00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:33.730
Which one?

00:19:33.805 --> 00:19:35.170
I, I don't know,
but we'll find him.

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:37.205
Everybody down!

00:19:42.347 --> 00:19:44.212
Base, we're under attack.

00:19:44.283 --> 00:19:46.148
Repeat, we're under attack.

00:19:46.218 --> 00:19:48.379
Those missing colonists,
they were armed.

00:19:48.453 --> 00:19:49.442
They fired the first shots.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:50.545
It wasn't our fault.

00:19:50.622 --> 00:19:51.919
You can't be sure of that.

00:19:52.057 --> 00:19:53.388
It could've been
one of our own people.

00:19:53.458 --> 00:19:55.358
Fatigue, a phaser
malfunction...

00:19:55.427 --> 00:19:56.394
you just don't know!

00:19:56.461 --> 00:19:59.919
Either way, it doesn't
justify what we did.

00:19:59.998 --> 00:20:01.727
What did you do?

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.926
What happened down there?

00:20:03.068 --> 00:20:04.330
Keep moving.

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:05.597
Stay together!

00:20:09.541 --> 00:20:10.508
Hold your fire!

00:20:13.545 --> 00:20:14.842
Stay down!

00:20:17.516 --> 00:20:18.483
Stay together!

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.484
Stop running! Stop!

00:20:20.552 --> 00:20:21.849
Get down!

00:20:24.423 --> 00:20:26.357
Get down! Get down!
Get down!

00:20:27.492 --> 00:20:28.754
Stop running!

00:20:31.263 --> 00:20:32.787
Stop running!

00:20:32.864 --> 00:20:35.264
Stop running!
Stop running!

00:20:36.501 --> 00:20:37.695
Stop running!

00:20:37.769 --> 00:20:39.669
I said stop!

00:20:39.738 --> 00:20:41.103
We didn't have any other choice.

00:20:41.173 --> 00:20:42.663
Like hell, we didn't.

00:20:42.741 --> 00:20:44.675
They were wiping us out!

00:20:44.743 --> 00:20:46.608
That didn't give us
the right to murder civilians.

00:20:46.678 --> 00:20:48.578
I tried to protect
the children,

00:20:48.647 --> 00:20:51.115
but I couldn't stop them
from running away.

00:20:51.183 --> 00:20:52.912
I ran, too.

00:20:52.985 --> 00:20:57.354
Sounds of phaser fire,
people shouting...

00:20:57.422 --> 00:20:58.946
I had to get out of there.

00:21:53.679 --> 00:21:55.374
Please, please, don't hurt us!

00:21:55.447 --> 00:21:58.177
Move out
where I can see you!

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:02.918
Move!

00:22:02.988 --> 00:22:05.855
Please. Please,
he's no threat to you.

00:22:06.925 --> 00:22:08.688
Tell me how I can
get out of these tunnels,

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.125
and I'll leave you alone.

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:13.290
Tell me!

00:22:13.365 --> 00:22:15.595
Oh! Go back the way you came.

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:18.363
At the second fork,
take the tunnel to your left,

00:22:18.437 --> 00:22:20.302
follow it to the end.

00:22:20.372 --> 00:22:22.203
It will lead you to the river.

00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:31.778
He was going to kill me.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:33.249
Easy, Harry.

00:22:33.318 --> 00:22:34.410
They wouldn't listen!

00:22:34.486 --> 00:22:35.475
Why?

00:22:35.554 --> 00:22:37.249
Why wouldn't they listen?

00:22:39.458 --> 00:22:42.894
We killed 82 civilians
that night.

00:22:42.961 --> 00:22:45.953
No one was left alive.

00:22:52.237 --> 00:22:54.205
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:54.272 --> 00:22:55.432
We've entered the system

00:22:55.507 --> 00:22:57.839
where the away team
conducted its recent survey,

00:22:57.909 --> 00:22:59.342
hoping to find an explanation

00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:01.606
for their memories
of the Nakan massacre.

00:23:07.152 --> 00:23:08.517
Yeah.

00:23:09.554 --> 00:23:11.385
Yeah!

00:23:16.395 --> 00:23:18.192
Missed you at breakfast.

00:23:18.263 --> 00:23:20.925
I wasn't hungry.

00:23:21.032 --> 00:23:23.660
Sleep a little?

00:23:23.735 --> 00:23:27.535
Five... six minutes.

00:23:27.606 --> 00:23:31.474
I found another episode
of The Untouchables.

00:23:31.543 --> 00:23:35.809
Eliot Ness captures
someone named Al Cay-pone.

00:23:35.881 --> 00:23:37.940
"Capone."

00:23:38.049 --> 00:23:39.448
Maybe later.

00:23:43.655 --> 00:23:44.917
Well, you've got
to eat something.

00:23:44.990 --> 00:23:46.287
Pizza?

00:23:46.358 --> 00:23:49.691
Look, I appreciate what
you're trying to do,

00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:51.285
but I'd rather just be alone.

00:23:53.432 --> 00:23:54.399
Tom...

00:23:54.466 --> 00:23:55.490
No!

00:23:55.567 --> 00:24:00.231
I don't want to be...
comforted right now.

00:24:03.041 --> 00:24:04.668
I know the last few days
have been difficult.

00:24:04.743 --> 00:24:06.540
Oh. "Difficult."

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:09.239
"Difficult" doesn't
quite cover it.

00:24:09.314 --> 00:24:12.647
I helped murder
82 innocent people.

00:24:12.717 --> 00:24:13.775
You don't know that.

00:24:13.852 --> 00:24:14.784
I know what I remember.

00:24:14.853 --> 00:24:15.785
The Doctor says your memories

00:24:15.854 --> 00:24:16.786
could have been altered.

00:24:16.855 --> 00:24:18.152
I was there!

00:24:18.223 --> 00:24:21.351
When I close my eyes,
I can see the bodies.

00:24:21.426 --> 00:24:23.690
I-I can hear
the weapons fire!

00:24:23.762 --> 00:24:25.161
I can feel
where I was shot!

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:26.754
Then why isn't there
evidence of a war?

00:24:26.832 --> 00:24:28.163
I don't know!

00:24:28.233 --> 00:24:31.600
All I'm asking is that you
consider the possibility

00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:34.935
that this didn't happen.

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:36.803
We'll keep investigating.

00:24:36.875 --> 00:24:38.934
There are sensor readings
on the Delta Flyer

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:40.272
that we haven't
even analyzed yet.

00:24:40.345 --> 00:24:43.610
I-I can't concentrate
on sensor readings right now.

00:24:43.682 --> 00:24:44.910
Try.

00:24:44.983 --> 00:24:46.848
I can't! Stop pushing me!

00:24:46.918 --> 00:24:49.887
I don't want your help!

00:24:53.558 --> 00:24:56.152
I'm sorry.

00:24:56.228 --> 00:24:59.254
You know where to find me.

00:25:04.803 --> 00:25:07.203
This was your first
stop on the away mission,

00:25:07.272 --> 00:25:08.398
a Class-M planet

00:25:08.473 --> 00:25:09.633
with one natural satellite.

00:25:09.708 --> 00:25:11.300
Did you send anyone
to the surface?

00:25:11.376 --> 00:25:13.310
No, we only scanned
for dilithium deposits.

00:25:13.378 --> 00:25:15.209
We were in orbit
for less than an hour.

00:25:15.280 --> 00:25:16.247
Next.

00:25:17.215 --> 00:25:19.445
You came into contact
with this vessel

00:25:19.518 --> 00:25:21.076
en route to your second

00:25:21.152 --> 00:25:22.449
destination.

00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:24.751
Captain Bathar of Hodos.

00:25:24.823 --> 00:25:26.085
Photogenic.

00:25:26.157 --> 00:25:27.556
He's a merchant.

00:25:27.626 --> 00:25:30.823
Claimed to have a formula
that stops the aging process.

00:25:30.896 --> 00:25:33.262
Oh, you didn't happen
to buy any, did you?

00:25:33.331 --> 00:25:35.322
It was only
a tripolymer enzyme.

00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:37.391
Makes great
shoe polish, though.

00:25:37.469 --> 00:25:38.458
Moving on.

00:25:39.604 --> 00:25:40.969
Your second stop.

00:25:45.777 --> 00:25:47.870
Tarakis.

00:25:53.285 --> 00:25:55.776
The planet, it's called Tarakis.

00:25:56.955 --> 00:25:58.684
I've been here.

00:26:33.725 --> 00:26:35.317
What the hell
are you doing?!

00:26:35.393 --> 00:26:36.325
Stand aside.

00:26:36.394 --> 00:26:37.554
They're already dead!

00:26:37.629 --> 00:26:38.721
They were never here.

00:26:38.797 --> 00:26:40.287
We disabled their
shield generators,

00:26:40.365 --> 00:26:42.595
entered the colony
and they were gone.

00:26:42.667 --> 00:26:44.794
No one's going
to believe that.

00:26:44.869 --> 00:26:46.666
They will if we all
keep to the same story.

00:26:46.738 --> 00:26:48.262
I won't lie about
what happened here.

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:49.671
Then you say nothing.

00:26:49.741 --> 00:26:51.038
We murdered these people!

00:26:51.109 --> 00:26:52.235
In self-defense!

00:26:52.310 --> 00:26:53.538
If that were true, you wouldn't

00:26:53.612 --> 00:26:54.704
be vaporizing the evidence!

00:26:54.779 --> 00:26:56.508
You don't have
to listen to him.

00:26:56.581 --> 00:26:58.242
We've got to let people know.

00:26:58.316 --> 00:27:00.147
We panicked!
They'll understand!

00:27:00.218 --> 00:27:01.150
No, they won't!

00:27:01.219 --> 00:27:02.186
Move away.

00:27:02.253 --> 00:27:03.220
I said

00:27:03.288 --> 00:27:04.152
move away!

00:27:25.110 --> 00:27:26.907
How long have I been here?

00:27:27.045 --> 00:27:28.342
Three hours.

00:27:28.413 --> 00:27:31.405
You started hallucinating
in Astrometrics.

00:27:31.483 --> 00:27:33.974
I'm afraid I had to sedate you.

00:27:35.920 --> 00:27:37.410
I was there.

00:27:37.489 --> 00:27:41.823
I was at the colony...

00:27:41.893 --> 00:27:43.690
with Saavdra.

00:27:43.762 --> 00:27:45.525
You're not the only one.

00:27:45.597 --> 00:27:47.861
39 crew members
have begun to experience

00:27:47.932 --> 00:27:50.093
the same memories.

00:27:50.168 --> 00:27:51.465
It appears
that the entire crew

00:27:51.536 --> 00:27:53.663
has been affected.

00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:14.215
Their symptoms are identical...

00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:19.195
increased engramatic
activity, nightmares.

00:28:19.264 --> 00:28:21.198
I can imagine the away team

00:28:21.266 --> 00:28:23.530
being pulled
into an alien conflict.

00:28:23.601 --> 00:28:27.560
But these people weren't
anywhere near this system.

00:28:27.639 --> 00:28:30.506
We've analyzed Voyager's
sensor records.

00:28:30.575 --> 00:28:32.167
If we did participate
in a war,

00:28:32.243 --> 00:28:34.768
all evidence of it
has been erased.

00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:36.905
The dream was so vivid...

00:28:37.048 --> 00:28:38.538
as real as anything

00:28:38.616 --> 00:28:40.811
I've experienced.

00:28:40.885 --> 00:28:43.945
But I refuse to believe
that we could...

00:28:45.824 --> 00:28:47.382
Real or not, the memories

00:28:47.459 --> 00:28:49.757
are having a deleterious effect
on the crew.

00:28:49.828 --> 00:28:52.854
The syndrome began to spread
once we entered this system.

00:28:52.931 --> 00:28:54.899
I suggest we reverse course,

00:28:54.966 --> 00:28:56.433
before it gets worse.

00:28:56.501 --> 00:29:02.303
No. If this massacre really
happened, someone is to blame.

00:29:02.373 --> 00:29:05.137
I want to be certain
that it wasn't us.

00:29:05.210 --> 00:29:07.144
With all due respect,
your judgment

00:29:07.212 --> 00:29:09.146
may be clouded by
feelings of guilt

00:29:09.214 --> 00:29:11.478
about an incident
that never occurred.

00:29:11.549 --> 00:29:12.846
The danger to our crew

00:29:12.917 --> 00:29:16.546
here and now, is indisputable.

00:29:16.621 --> 00:29:20.079
I've seen you
looking better, Ensign.

00:29:20.158 --> 00:29:22.422
Yes, ma'am.

00:29:22.494 --> 00:29:25.292
I've felt better myself,

00:29:25.363 --> 00:29:27.957
but we're going
to get through this.

00:29:39.944 --> 00:29:41.741
The massacre took
place on Tarakis.

00:29:41.813 --> 00:29:43.405
Go to Red Alert
and set a course.

00:29:43.481 --> 00:29:44.413
Aye, Captain.

00:29:44.482 --> 00:29:45.813
A neural suppressant.

00:29:45.884 --> 00:29:48.546
It'll help keep
the memories from resurfacing.

00:30:02.333 --> 00:30:04.096
Your favorites...

00:30:04.169 --> 00:30:07.195
Talaxian stew
and terra nut soufflé.

00:30:07.272 --> 00:30:08.864
The soufflé
has collapsed slightly,

00:30:08.940 --> 00:30:10.805
but its nutritional content
is intact.

00:30:10.875 --> 00:30:13.173
Thank you.

00:30:13.244 --> 00:30:14.905
It looks delicious.

00:30:16.514 --> 00:30:20.280
When Naomi Wildman is sad,
she consumes desserts.

00:30:20.351 --> 00:30:23.650
She claims it improves
her emotional state.

00:30:23.721 --> 00:30:25.279
Perhaps you should try it.

00:30:25.356 --> 00:30:27.256
Naomi must be terrified of me...

00:30:27.325 --> 00:30:29.452
after what happened
in the galley.

00:30:29.527 --> 00:30:32.189
She's concerned about you.

00:30:32.263 --> 00:30:34.254
She told me she wants
to visit you.

00:30:34.332 --> 00:30:38.860
No, not like this.

00:30:38.937 --> 00:30:41.633
I might do something
to scare her again.

00:30:41.706 --> 00:30:43.901
I'll give her your regards.

00:30:46.945 --> 00:30:48.173
Seven...

00:30:52.717 --> 00:30:54.275
When you were a Borg,

00:30:54.352 --> 00:30:59.483
you were involved in some...
unpleasant activities.

00:30:59.557 --> 00:31:01.752
I helped to assimilate millions.

00:31:01.826 --> 00:31:04.590
I don't mean to be insensitive,

00:31:04.662 --> 00:31:11.761
but... do you ever feel shame
about what you did?

00:31:11.836 --> 00:31:12.928
Frequently.

00:31:13.071 --> 00:31:15.733
How do you manage
to keep going,

00:31:15.807 --> 00:31:19.868
knowing that you've done
such horrible things?

00:31:19.944 --> 00:31:21.639
I have no choice.

00:31:23.348 --> 00:31:24.781
Guilt is irrelevant?

00:31:24.849 --> 00:31:28.216
On the contrary,
my feelings of remorse

00:31:28.286 --> 00:31:30.686
help me remember what I did

00:31:30.755 --> 00:31:33.315
and prevent me from taking
similar actions in the future.

00:31:35.426 --> 00:31:38.884
Guilt can be a difficult
but useful emotion.

00:31:42.533 --> 00:31:45.502
It's certainly difficult.

00:31:49.040 --> 00:31:52.976
Is that chocolate mixed in there
with the terra nuts?

00:31:53.111 --> 00:31:55.511
I altered the recipe slightly.

00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:57.480
I hope you don't object.

00:31:57.548 --> 00:32:00.847
Not at all.

00:32:15.333 --> 00:32:16.800
Tarakis, dead ahead.

00:32:16.868 --> 00:32:17.800
Shields.

00:32:17.869 --> 00:32:19.803
Stand by weapons.

00:32:19.871 --> 00:32:20.838
On screen.

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:25.205
Scan for vessels.

00:32:25.276 --> 00:32:27.073
There are none.

00:32:27.145 --> 00:32:29.477
Take us into orbit.

00:32:29.547 --> 00:32:30.946
Ma'am?

00:32:31.082 --> 00:32:32.413
Do it, Mr. Paris.

00:32:41.559 --> 00:32:43.083
Life signs?

00:32:43.161 --> 00:32:45.857
The planet appears
to be uninhabited.

00:32:45.930 --> 00:32:47.363
Looks the same as it did
a few days ago,

00:32:47.432 --> 00:32:48.865
when we scanned
for dilithium deposits.

00:32:48.933 --> 00:32:51.094
Signs of weapons fire
or phaser residue?

00:32:51.169 --> 00:32:52.261
Negative.

00:32:52.337 --> 00:32:55.602
Run a full spectral scan.

00:32:55.673 --> 00:32:57.436
Look for anything unusual.

00:32:57.508 --> 00:33:00.534
Nothing on geometric sensors.

00:33:00.611 --> 00:33:01.543
Hold on.

00:33:01.612 --> 00:33:03.239
I'm picking up
a power signature.

00:33:03.314 --> 00:33:05.009
- Source?
- I can't tell.

00:33:05.083 --> 00:33:06.448
The signal's erratic,

00:33:06.517 --> 00:33:09.748
but it's coming
from the northernmost continent,

00:33:09.821 --> 00:33:11.049
coordinates 172

00:33:11.122 --> 00:33:13.181
mark 5.

00:33:25.937 --> 00:33:27.404
Phasers.

00:33:39.450 --> 00:33:40.883
Call it an educated guess,

00:33:40.952 --> 00:33:44.115
but I don't think this
looks like a war zone.

00:33:44.188 --> 00:33:45.883
There's something familiar
about it though.

00:33:45.957 --> 00:33:47.891
I recognize those mountains.

00:33:47.959 --> 00:33:50.189
Those trees weren't here.

00:33:50.261 --> 00:33:51.956
Search the area.

00:34:14.352 --> 00:34:16.547
Ensign?

00:34:16.621 --> 00:34:18.521
The tunnel.

00:34:18.589 --> 00:34:20.853
It's nearby.

00:34:20.925 --> 00:34:23.018
The one where I, uh...

00:34:24.662 --> 00:34:26.323
How'd you get into it?

00:34:26.397 --> 00:34:28.524
There was a rock formation.

00:34:28.599 --> 00:34:30.123
It hid the opening.

00:34:38.676 --> 00:34:41.144
A faint energy signature.

00:34:44.515 --> 00:34:46.278
This way.

00:35:04.402 --> 00:35:06.370
Over here.

00:35:26.324 --> 00:35:27.757
There's your
physical evidence.

00:35:27.825 --> 00:35:30.089
I suggest we proceed
with caution.

00:35:30.161 --> 00:35:31.958
Stand guard.

00:36:04.795 --> 00:36:06.319
I... I... I can't.

00:36:06.397 --> 00:36:08.365
Remain calm.

00:36:08.432 --> 00:36:11.697
Slow, deep breaths.

00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:45.131
They were over there.

00:36:58.282 --> 00:37:00.250
I found the remains
of two humanoids,

00:37:00.318 --> 00:37:02.946
but you were not responsible
for their deaths.

00:37:04.555 --> 00:37:07.649
They died over 300 years ago.

00:38:04.415 --> 00:38:07.043
I think we found our war.

00:38:12.923 --> 00:38:16.086
The structure contains
a synaptic transmitter.

00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:17.092
I believe it was designed

00:38:17.161 --> 00:38:18.890
to send neurogenic pulses

00:38:19.030 --> 00:38:20.725
throughout this system.

00:38:20.798 --> 00:38:22.425
So anyone passing through

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:24.593
would experience
the Nakan massacre...

00:38:24.669 --> 00:38:25.829
like we did.

00:38:25.903 --> 00:38:27.302
Precisely.

00:38:27.371 --> 00:38:30.204
Try running those symbols
inscribed on the base

00:38:30.274 --> 00:38:32.208
through the translation matrix.

00:38:35.846 --> 00:38:38.906
"Words alone cannot
convey the suffering.

00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:40.507
"Words alone cannot prevent

00:38:40.584 --> 00:38:42.916
"what happened here
from happening again.

00:38:43.020 --> 00:38:45.921
"Beyond words lies experience.

00:38:46.023 --> 00:38:49.117
"Beyond experience lies truth.

00:38:49.193 --> 00:38:51.593
"Make this truth

00:38:51.662 --> 00:38:53.061
your own."

00:38:53.130 --> 00:38:56.258
It's a memorial.

00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:59.235
We weren't victims
of a conspiracy.

00:38:59.303 --> 00:39:01.498
We were witnesses to a massacre.

00:39:01.572 --> 00:39:03.005
More than witnesses.

00:39:03.074 --> 00:39:04.871
By being forced
to relive those events,

00:39:04.942 --> 00:39:06.500
half the crew's
been traumatized.

00:39:06.577 --> 00:39:08.238
Maybe that was the point.

00:39:08.312 --> 00:39:11.247
I certainly won't forget
what happened here.

00:39:11.315 --> 00:39:14.375
Anything in that database
that might tell us who built

00:39:14.452 --> 00:39:15.578
this thing?

00:39:15.653 --> 00:39:17.587
No. The technology
has been neglected

00:39:17.655 --> 00:39:19.247
for more than two centuries.

00:39:19.323 --> 00:39:21.257
Its power cells
are deteriorating.

00:39:21.325 --> 00:39:22.553
That could explain

00:39:22.626 --> 00:39:25.117
why our memories
were so fragmented.

00:39:25.196 --> 00:39:26.595
It was probably designed

00:39:26.664 --> 00:39:28.894
to transmit the experience
in sequence.

00:39:28.999 --> 00:39:31.194
Fascinating.
Now let's try to shut it down

00:39:31.268 --> 00:39:33.327
so nobody else
has to go through this.

00:39:35.406 --> 00:39:36.668
Kathryn?

00:39:38.209 --> 00:39:39.506
Yes, of course.

00:39:41.345 --> 00:39:44.542
Even if we do shut down
the transmitter,

00:39:44.615 --> 00:39:47.641
I'm afraid your memories
of the massacre are permanent.

00:39:47.718 --> 00:39:49.276
But we'll prevent this
from happening

00:39:49.353 --> 00:39:50.445
to other passing ships.

00:39:50.521 --> 00:39:51.920
If we do that, all record

00:39:52.022 --> 00:39:54.149
of what happened here
would be lost.

00:39:54.225 --> 00:39:55.783
The monument
will still be here.

00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:57.919
But that doesn't really
tell the story.

00:39:58.028 --> 00:40:00.019
Someone put a lot
of time and care

00:40:00.097 --> 00:40:01.621
into building
that transmitter.

00:40:01.699 --> 00:40:02.723
We can't just

00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:03.732
deactivate it.

00:40:03.801 --> 00:40:05.029
We don't have the right.

00:40:05.102 --> 00:40:07.536
Did they have the right
to force us to relive all that?

00:40:07.605 --> 00:40:10.301
They wanted others to know
what it was like, in the hopes

00:40:10.374 --> 00:40:11.705
that nothing like it
would happen again.

00:40:11.776 --> 00:40:13.334
Why should anyone
have to experience

00:40:13.411 --> 00:40:15.140
an atrocity they didn't commit?

00:40:15.212 --> 00:40:18.648
Because that's how you learn
not to make the same mistake.

00:40:18.716 --> 00:40:22.152
If we destroy the evidence,
we're no better than Saavdra.

00:40:22.219 --> 00:40:23.481
Maybe he had a point.

00:40:23.554 --> 00:40:25.146
It wasn't our fault.

00:40:25.222 --> 00:40:26.280
Given the danger
involved,

00:40:26.357 --> 00:40:27.847
it's only logical...

00:40:27.925 --> 00:40:29.222
This isn't about logic!

00:40:29.293 --> 00:40:30.658
It's about remembering!

00:40:30.728 --> 00:40:32.195
Some things are best forgotten.

00:40:32.263 --> 00:40:33.230
Not this.

00:40:35.166 --> 00:40:37.862
I stood by once before
and did nothing.

00:40:37.935 --> 00:40:38.959
Not again.

00:40:39.069 --> 00:40:40.297
Captain?

00:40:40.371 --> 00:40:42.566
I watched while Saavdra
vaporized the bodies.

00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:46.974
No offense, but those were
other people's memories.

00:40:47.077 --> 00:40:49.136
The Obelisk at Khitomer,

00:40:49.213 --> 00:40:50.373
the fields at Gettysburg,

00:40:50.448 --> 00:40:52.382
those were other people's
memories, too,

00:40:52.450 --> 00:40:54.179
but we don't
honor them any less.

00:40:54.251 --> 00:40:57.982
The 82 colonists
who died here...

00:40:59.690 --> 00:41:01.521
they deserve their memorial.

00:41:01.592 --> 00:41:03.184
Captain...

00:41:03.260 --> 00:41:05.421
We're not going to shut down
the transmitter. Is that clear?

00:41:07.465 --> 00:41:09.228
Is that clear?

00:41:09.300 --> 00:41:11.131
Are you suggesting

00:41:11.202 --> 00:41:12.169
we leave it intact?

00:41:12.236 --> 00:41:14.796
I'm suggesting
that we repair it.

00:41:14.872 --> 00:41:16.533
Recharge the power cells.

00:41:16.607 --> 00:41:17.938
I want that monument

00:41:18.008 --> 00:41:20.875
to function properly
for another 300 years.

00:41:20.945 --> 00:41:23.072
We'll place
a warning buoy in orbit.

00:41:23.147 --> 00:41:26.548
Anyone who enters this system
will know what to expect.

00:41:27.918 --> 00:41:29.283
Dismissed.

00:42:13.631 --> 00:42:15.258
We're ready, Captain.

00:42:19.169 --> 00:42:22.161
I know this was hardest
on the four of you,

00:42:22.239 --> 00:42:25.106
but if you hadn't
stopped at this planet,

00:42:25.175 --> 00:42:29.168
all the people who died here
would have been forgotten.

00:42:29.246 --> 00:42:33.239
And if they could,
I know they'd thank you.

00:42:34.885 --> 00:42:36.750
Janeway to Voyager.

00:42:36.820 --> 00:42:39.414
Stand by to initiate
power transfer.

00:42:41.959 --> 00:42:43.688
Five to beam up.
